keys:

    ctrl+t (or ctrl+n)      new shell tab
    ctrl+w                  close tab
    ctrl+→/← (or ctrl+f/b)  next / previous tab


install to `~/.local/bin/tabs`:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/install.sh | bash


update with:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/update.sh | bash


make sure `~/.local/bin` is on your path, then run `tabs`.
to use `tabs` when you type `tmux`, add `alias tmux=tabs` to your shell config.
`command tmux` still runs the real tmux.


agent status:

    Claude Code, Codex CLI and Pi show a blinking dot while working.
    Tabs turn green when an agent finishes or requests input.
    Agent status is cleared on session exit.

installing or updating tabs configures the agent hooks automatically.
Pi uses `~/.pi/agent/extensions/tmux-tabs.js` (or the agent directory set
by `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`). Restart Pi or run `/reload` after installation.
The Pi hook only tracks interactive runs inside tabs, not print/JSON/RPC runs.
Pi completion uses the `agent_settled` extension event so retries and queued
follow-ups remain marked as working. A Pi version supporting that event is required.
